# 1️⃣ Frog Jump K Distance

## Problem

Frog can jump:

```text
1 to K steps
```

at a time.

Energy Cost:

```text
abs(
height[i]
-
height[j]
)
```

Find minimum energy.

---

### Example

```text
10 30 40 50 20

K = 3
```

---

# 2️⃣ Recurrence

For every position:

```cpp
dp[i]
=
min(
all possible jumps
)
```

Formula:

```cpp
dp[i] =
min(
dp[i-j]
+
abs(
h[i]
-
h[i-j]
)
)
```

where:

```text
1 ≤ j ≤ K
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N*K)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Maximum Sum of Non Adjacent Elements

## Problem

Find:

```text
Maximum Sum
```

without taking adjacent elements.

---

### Example

```text
2 1 4 9
```

Answer:

```text
11
```

Choose:

```text
2 + 9
```

---

# 4️⃣ Recurrence

### Pick

```cpp
arr[i]
+
dp[i-2]
```

### Not Pick

```cpp
dp[i-1]
```

Formula:

```cpp
dp[i]
=
max(
pick,
notPick
)
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 5️⃣ House Robber II

## Problem

Houses are arranged in:

```text
Circle
```

First and last house become adjacent.

---

### Example

```text
2 3 2
```

Answer:

```text
3
```

---

# 6️⃣ Observation

Cannot take:

```text
First House
and
Last House
Together
```

Solve:

### Case 1

```text
Exclude First House
```

### Case 2

```text
Exclude Last House
```

Apply:

```text
House Robber I
```

Take maximum.

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 7️⃣ Ninja Training

## Problem

For each day:

```text
3 Activities
```

Cannot perform same activity on consecutive days.

---

### Example

```text
Day 1

10 40 70

Day 2

20 50 80

Day 3

30 60 90
```

Output:

```text
210
```

---

# 8️⃣ State Definition

State:

```cpp
dp[day][last]
```

Meaning:

```text
Maximum points till day
if last activity was "last"
```

---

### Recurrence

Try all activities except:

```text
last
```

Take maximum.

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N × 4 × 3)

Space: O(N × 4)
```

---

# 9️⃣ Grid DP Introduction

Most Grid DP Problems involve:

```text
Move Right

